  "id": "depth-psychology",
  "term": "depth psychology",
  "definition": "Depth psychology is a psychoanalytic or psychodynamic approach that works with hard-to-express inner experience, such as feelings, bodily sensations, and fragmentary thoughts linked to significant events. In this context, it aims to help people form a more organized understanding of those experiences and their effects on current life.",
